# Update JRebirth Site Documentation

Keep the Maven Site documentation in sync whenever framework code changes. Documentation that drifts from the code confuses contributors and users.

## Location

All documentation pages live under `org.jrebirth.af/src/site/markdown/doc/`.

The format is Markdown with Velocity (`.md.vm`). Velocity macros control navigation, table of contents, and live code snippet includes.

## Sync checklist (run through this when code changes)

1. Identify which documentation page covers the changed module or feature. Use the module-to-page map in `reference.md`.
2. If no page covers the change, create a new one.
3. Update or add `MACRO{include}` snippets pointing to the changed source files.
4. Verify that snippet selectors still match. Method or class renames break `aj:` selectors — update them.
5. Update the prose to reflect new behavior, new parameters, or changed annotations.
6. If a new module is added, also update `TocList.vm`, `site.xml`, and `jrebirth-book.xml`.

## Style rules

- Write clear, direct prose. Avoid filler phrases like "it is important to note that" or "please be aware".
- Use `**bold**` for a class or annotation name on its first mention in a section.
- Keep code snippets sourced from real files via `MACRO{include}` rather than hand-written. This ensures examples stay accurate when the code changes.
- Place body content inside a `#[[ ]]#` block to prevent Velocity from parsing it.

For the page template, snippet selector syntax, new-page steps, and the module-to-page map, see `reference.md`.
